    "geometry_type": "real",
    "digitized_from": "OpenStreetMap (ways 149253142 and 288671185, addr:housename=The Beacon, 250 & 260 King St)",
    "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-18 for Mission Bay's second real-site pass: real, address-tagged OpenStreetMap building footprints for both towers of The Beacon (250 King St and 260 King St), one of the first major Mission Bay North residential developments (Catellus, ~595 units, completed circa 2003-2004). Registered as a single MultiPolygon record for the one named complex, mirroring how this project already combines multi-part named features (e.g. Pier 70's Irish Hill Playground and Irish Hill Corner Plaza).",
    "accuracy_caveat": "REAL -- surveyed OpenStreetMap building footprint(s), not a hand trace or plan estimate. The underlying Assessor parcel is condo-mapped across many individually owned per-unit lots (confirmed against data/raw/parcels.geojson), so no single blklot represents the whole building and it cannot be joined via status.csv the way a single-owner parcel can. Using the real building footprint from OSM instead of a fabricated or arbitrarily chosen 'representative' unit lot, the same real-geometry-without-a-single-parcel pattern already used for several Pier 70 buildings (DataSF Building Footprints) and for Mission Bay's own real park polygons.",
    "notes": "Full-block mixed-use condominium complex at 250/260 King St; ground-floor retail (grocery, bank, spa) below residential floors. Architect attribution conflicts between sources (Brand + Allen Architects per one architect-portfolio source vs. SOM/HKS per an aggregator) and is not resolved here -- not recorded as a fact pending a primary-source confirmation.",
